content.text:
All 9 units of the plan are built, and PR #1 is open: https://github.com/hayagreev2003/task-list-app/pull/1 (pushed as `hayagreev2003`).

**Checks:** `npm test` passes 112 tests: unit tests plus integration tests against local Supabase. TypeScript, ESLint and `next build` are clean. A fresh clone set up using only the README also gets green tests and a clean build. One caveat: local Supabase was already running when I did that, so first-time image downloads weren't part of it.

**RLS check:** with row-level security switched off on the tasks table, 4 of the isolation tests fail. With it back on, they pass. The README explains how to repeat this.

**In the browser** I went through:
- sign-up, sign-in (including a wrong password) and sign-out;
- creating, editing, completing and deleting tasks (with an inline delete confirmation);
- search and filters;
- importing `samples/edge-case.csv` and downloading the rejected rows;
- every file-level error (empty, not a CSV, missing column, over 1 MB, not UTF-8);
- a second user, who sees only an empty list.

**Changes from the plan:**
- **Node 22 is now required.** The current Supabase JS library needs a built-in WebSocket that Node 20 doesn't have. I added `.nvmrc` and the `engines` field, and the README says Node 22+.
- **A Next.js 16 warning in dev.** The Supabase library reads the current time while pages are being prerendered. Next.js flagged this; making the session read always happen at request time fixed it.
- **Fixes from a security review.** The review found no way for one user to reach another user's tasks. I acted on the smaller points:
  - formula-like cells in the rejected-rows download now get a leading `'` so spreadsheets don't run them;
  - notes are capped at 2,000 characters, in the app and in a new database migration;
  - the sign-up error no longer reveals whether an email already has an account;
  - the local minimum password length is now 8.

  Two minor issues are listed as known limitations in the README: `*` acts as a wildcard in search, and rare Unicode titles can get the wrong duplicate reason.

**Still to do:**
- `ai-log/` is not included, as you asked. The PR and README say it will follow after a privacy check.
- The screen recording link in the README is a placeholder.
- I didn't upload screenshots to a public image host for the PR.
- Before any hosted deploy: run `npx supabase db push` and set the minimum password length to 8 on the hosted project.
- The local database still has the manual test accounts `alice@example.test` and `bob@example.test`. `npm run db:reset` clears them.

The dev server may still be running on port 3100: stopping it returned a non-zero exit code and I didn't check further.
